# True Creation - union of the .gitignore files from PalCreationEngine, PalItemgen and Palworld Server.

# Unity generated
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
/[Rr]ecordings/

# Never commit these
/[Aa]ssets/AssetStoreTools*
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*
.vs/
.vsconfig
.vscode/
.gradle/
ExportedObj/
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.app
crashlytics-build.properties
sysinfo.txt

# IDE / build cruft
.idea/
*.csproj
*.unityproj
*.sln
*.slnx
*.suo
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# .NET verification harnesses (built outside Unity). The two hand-written harness project files
# must stay tracked even though *.csproj is ignored above.
!Tools/*/VerifyHarness/VerifyHarness.csproj
Tools/*/VerifyHarness/bin/
Tools/*/VerifyHarness/obj/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Palworld Server panel: never commit captured server config -- it contains AdminPassword,
# ServerPassword and PublicIP in plain text.
*PalWorldSettings*.ini
*.bak.ini
/Snapshots/
# The generated option schema currently embeds the live server's current values, including
# AdminPassword, ServerPassword and PublicIP. Keep it out of source control until
# generate_schema.py stops writing secret values.
/Assets/StreamingAssets/palworld_option_schema.json
/Assets/StreamingAssets/palworld_option_schema.json.meta
# harness-built test mod packages (regenerated by dotnet run)
Tools/*/TestPackages/
